---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Hero from '~/components/widgets/Hero.astro';
import { BUSINESS } from '~/utils/site';

const metadata = {
  title: 'Privacy notice',
  description: `How ${BUSINESS.name} uses your personal data and cookies on this website.`,
};

const lastUpdated = '3 November 2026';
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <Hero tagline="Your data" title="Privacy notice" subtitle={`Last updated: ${lastUpdated}`} />

  <section
    class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pb-20 md:pb-28 prose prose-lg font-light prose-p:text-chocolate prose-li:text-chocolate prose-strong:text-chocolate prose-strong:font-medium prose-a:text-chocolate prose-a:underline-offset-4 prose-headings:font-heading prose-headings:font-normal prose-headings:text-chocolate prose-h2:text-5xl prose-h2:leading-[1.1] prose-h2:mb-4 prose-th:text-chocolate prose-th:font-medium prose-td:text-chocolate"
  >
    <p>
      This notice tells you what personal data we collect when you use this website, why we collect it, and what your
      rights are. It covers this website only.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      {BUSINESS.name} is a hair salon at {BUSINESS.address.join(', ')}. We are the controller of the personal data
      described in this notice. If you have a question about your data, email us at <a href={`mailto:${BUSINESS.email}`}
        >{BUSINESS.email}</a
      > or write to us at the salon address.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>When you send us a message</strong> with the contact form: your name, email address, phone number (if you
        give it) and your message.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>When you email or phone us</strong>: your contact details and what you tell us.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>When you visit the website</strong>: our hosting provider records technical data, such as your IP
        address, browser type and the pages you ask for. This is necessary to deliver the website and keep it secure.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>If you accept analytics cookies</strong>: Google Analytics collects data about how you use the website,
        such as the pages you visit, how long you stay, the type of device and browser, and your approximate location
        (town or region). Google Analytics does not give us your name or contact details.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not use advertising tools, and we do not sell your data.</p>

    <h2>Why we use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>To answer your message and arrange appointments.</strong> Our lawful basis is that you asked us to do this
        before you book with us, and our legitimate interest in replying to people who contact us.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>To run the website and keep it secure.</strong> Our lawful basis is our legitimate interest in a website
        that works and is safe.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>To understand how people use the website, so that we can improve it.</strong> Our lawful basis is your consent.
        You can withdraw it at any time in the cookie settings.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>We use these service providers. They process data for us only as needed to provide their service:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts this website and processes technical data such as IP addresses. See the <a
          href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare privacy policy</a
        >.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Our contact form provider</strong> receives your form message and sends it to us by email.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google</strong> provides Google Analytics and the map on our home and contact pages. Each one loads only
        if you accept its cookies. See the <a
          href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">Google privacy policy</a
        >.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>Some of these providers can process data outside the UK. When they do, they use legal safeguards for it.</p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      We keep your messages only for as long as we need them to answer you and arrange your appointment. We then delete
      them, and we do not keep them for more than 12 months.
    </p>

    <h2 id="cookies">Cookies</h2>
    <p>We ask before we use any cookies that are not strictly necessary. You can accept or reject each type:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Analytics</strong>: Google Analytics, to count visits and see which pages are useful.</li>
      <li><strong>Maps</strong>: Google Maps, to show where the salon is.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Our website also stores one setting in your browser to remember your choice. If you reject analytics cookies after
      you accepted them, we stop Google Analytics and delete its cookies.
    </p>
    <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8">
      <table class="w-full text-left text-base">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-gold">
            <th class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium">Name</th>
            <th class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium">Set by</th>
            <th class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium">Purpose</th>
            <th class="py-3 font-medium">Kept for</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="font-light divide-y divide-gold/40">
          <tr>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 align-top"><code class="text-sm">hs-cookie-consent</code></td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 align-top">This website (browser storage)</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 align-top">Remembers which cookies you accepted or rejected. Strictly necessary.</td>
            <td class="py-3 align-top">Until you clear your browser data</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 align-top"><code class="text-sm">_ga</code></td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 align-top">Google Analytics</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 align-top"
              >Tells visitors apart, so that we can count visits. Only if you accept analytics.</td
            >
            <td class="py-3 align-top">2 years</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 align-top"><code class="text-sm">_ga_&lt;ID&gt;</code></td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 align-top">Google Analytics</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 align-top">Keeps the state of your visit. Only if you accept analytics.</td>
            <td class="py-3 align-top">2 years</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 align-top">Google cookies</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 align-top">Google (Google Maps)</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 align-top">Set by Google when the map loads. Only if you accept maps.</td>
            <td class="py-3 align-top">See Google's policy</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      You can change your choice at any time: <button
        type="button"
        data-cookie-settings
        class="underline underline-offset-4 font-normal">open cookie settings</button
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under UK data protection law, you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>ask for a copy of your personal data</li>
      <li>ask us to correct data that is wrong</li>
      <li>ask us to delete your data</li>
      <li>ask us to limit how we use your data</li>
      <li>object to how we use your data</li>
      <li>ask us to send your data to another organisation</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To use any of these rights, email <a href={`mailto:${BUSINESS.email}`}>{BUSINESS.email}</a>. We reply within one
      month.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you are not happy with how we use your data, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) at <a
        href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk</a
      > or on 0303 123 1113. Please contact us first, so that we can try to help.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
    <p>If we change this notice, we put the new version on this page and change the date at the top.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
